# text = And now I say unto you that this is the order after which I am called, yea, to preach unto my beloved brethren, yea, and every one that dwelleth in the land; yea, to preach unto all, both old and young, both bond and free; yea, I say unto you the aged, and also the middle aged, and the rising generation; yea, to cry unto them that they must repent and be born again.
# sent_id = 202
# llm_note = Long sentence. Root = "say"(4). ccomp: "this is the order after which I am called". The series of "yea, to preach...yea, to preach...yea, I say...yea, to cry" are coordinated elaborations of the main clause (appositive or conj elaborations on "called"/"order"). "yea, to preach"(21) = xcomp of "called"(16). "and every one that dwelleth" = conj of "my beloved brethren". "yea, to preach unto all, both old and young, both bond and free" = conj of first "preach". "yea, I say unto you the aged..." = conj of root "say". "yea, to cry unto them that they must repent and be born again" = conj of "preach"(41).
